{
  "_comment": [
    "Prop metadata shared by the runtime (src/art/PropDefinitions.ts) and the map",
    "generator (tools/build-map.mjs). One source of truth so a prop's gameplay",
    "collision can never disagree between build time and run time.",
    "",
    "Canvas dimensions and feetInset are MEASURED from the PNGs with",
    "tools/inspect-assets.py; every prop has exactly 1px of transparent padding",
    "below its content, so the ground-contact row is height-1.",
    "",
    "footprint is the gameplay collision box in pixels, centred on the prop's",
    "anchor x, with its bottom edge at the anchor y. It is deliberately much",
    "smaller than the sprite rectangle: a 32x32 tree is an 10x8 trunk, not a",
    "32x32 wall. A null footprint means no collision at all.",
    "",
    "depth: 'ground' draws below characters, 'sorted' is y-sorted with them (so a",
    "character south of a tree trunk draws in front of its canopy and one north",
    "of it draws behind), 'front' draws above them (overhead laundry, banners).",
    "",
    "cover: 'high' blocks sight and bullets; 'low' blocks bullets always and",
    "sight only of a crouched player; 'none' is solid but not cover."
  ],
